  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

All original copyright and license headers in the source files are retained.

Modifications in this fork (over doctor64/tuyaZigbee), in the `light` application and
device configuration, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0:
  - Rewrote the brightness curve (full-resolution gamma with a measured low-end floor,
    per-channel off at zero) to lower the usable minimum brightness.
  - Corrected the CCT pin/channel mapping for the ZB-CT01 board (cool = PB5/PWM5,
    warm = PB4/PWM4) and set the PWM frequency to 6 kHz.
  - Made brightness changes update both CCT channels while preserving color temperature.
  - Set the Zigbee model id to "ZB-CT01" for native Zigbee2MQTT support.
  - Mapped the physical button on PD3 (short press on/off, long press factory reset).
  - Configured a monolithic 512 KB build (CHIP_TYPE TLSR_8258_512K, BOOT_LOADER_MODE 0)
    flashed at 0x0 over SWire, preserving the factory MAC at 0x76000.

See README.md for details.
